    "summary": "High‑energy Seattle set with smoking Jack Straw and killer Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a smoking Jack Straw, an inventive Other One → Bobby McGee improvisation, and a tight Truckin'‑Drums‑Other One sequence. Jerry’s lead work shines on Playing In The Band while Phil supplies monster bass throughout. A soundboard source captures the high‑energy performance with excellent clarity.",
    "review": "June 26, 1973 at Seattle Center Arena finds the Dead in top form, rolling through a three‑plus hour marathon of over thirty songs without losing steam. The first set builds momentum with a rousing Jack Straw and a crisp Playing In The Band, while the China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue showcases Bob’s vocal fire and Jerry’s tasteful leads. The second set is where the night truly soars: Here Comes Sunshine lifts the mood before a powerhouse He's Gone launches into a seamless Truckin' → Drums → The Other One flow that bursts into an inventive Other One → Bobby McGee jam, highlighted by Keith’s splattering Rhodes textures. The encore rounds it out with a rollicking Johnny B. Goode, leaving the audience buzzing. Across the night Phil’s bass is relentless—especially on He's Gone and Playin' In The Band—while Mickey and Billy lock in tight, providing that extra umph noted in the soundboard capture. Overall, this Seattle gig stands as one of the season’s most vibrant performances.",
